      "title": "Scientific Integrity in Practice",
      "gist": "Historical cases—from Millikan's slowly corrected electron charge to public and political communication—show how easily scientists fool themselves, and how integrity resists that.",
      "question": "scientific integrity — how do scientists guard against fooling themselves and others? (several historical examples)"
    },
